  "name": "pendulum-triple-fixed",
  "$comment": "X5.11: a triple pendulum on a fixed pivot, driven at the first joint by a DC gearmotor (pendubot type). Multibond planar bond graph: RigidBody2D links with distributed mass, Revolute2DCompliant joints (kt = 1e8 N/m converges to the rigid revolute), the drive is stdlib drives/ElectricDrive -> ElasticShaft -> Gearbox -> joint 1. project:TriplePendCtrl swings the chain up along the optimised trajectory (time-varying LQR), catches it with a 1 kHz LQR and balances; a force pulse at the tip link at t = 8 s is the disturbance. Generated by design/build_model.py; the controller tables come from design/design.py.",
